NEARS-1115 — AC4/AC5 (store reviews) live verification notes
================================================================

BLOCKER (pre-existing, NOT part of this diff): on the current mobile store
screen, the rating "pill" rendered by NearsStoreHeaderSliver._MetaBlock
(UserApp/lib/features/store/widgets/nears_store_header_sliver.dart) has no
onTap handler — confirmed by reading the widget source (no `onTap:` wired to
the pill) and by a live Dart VM `ext.flutter.debugDumpRenderTree` dump of the
running app on the store screen, which shows no `Icons.star`/orange-colored
RenderObject subtree at all. The ONLY other caller of
RouteHelper.getStoreReviewRoute() is the OLD StoreDescriptionViewWidget,
which is dead code on mobile (ResponsiveHelper.isDesktop(context) branch only
— confirmed by reading store_description_view_widget.dart lines 37-154/223).
ReviewScreen is also not deep-linkable (LinkConverter.navigateFromLink only
recognizes /, /store, /item-details, /refer-and-earn prefixes — confirmed
live: an OS intent to /store-review/... logs
"deep link: unknown route, falling back to initial" and bounces to home).

Net effect: there is currently NO way for a real user to reach the Reviews
screen for ANY store on the reskinned mobile UserApp. Filed separately as a
regression_bug (pre-existing, unrelated to NEARS-1115's own diff).

Because of that blocker, AC4/AC5 could not be watched rendering live on
device. In its place, the exact HTTP contract ReviewRepository.getList()
consumes (`GET /api/v1/stores/reviews?store_id=<id>`) was exercised live
against the same backend the app is pointed at (127.0.0.1:8000, primary
Admin/ tree, 2026-07-17 10:30 local):

  store_id=12 (Fresh local — real, active, in-zone, 0 reviews in DB):
    HTTP 200 []
  store_id=999999 (unknown, matches the fixture the backend's own
    StoreDetailsNotFoundTest.php uses as UNKNOWN_ID):
    HTTP 404 {"errors":[{"code":"store_not_found","message":"Store not found"}]}
  store_id=4116 (NEARS-475 Fixture Store (Inactive) — real row, status=0):
    HTTP 404 {"errors":[{"code":"store_not_found","message":"Store not found"}]}

Matching backend laravel.log lines (Admin/storage/logs/laravel.log), same
run:
  [2026-07-17 10:30:43] production.ERROR: [FAIL] store reviews: store not
    found {"trace_id":"8734439425c5b9506fb596a666aa660b","correlation_id":
    "3a9f0771-3f48-46c9-a296-b3f707b6933f","endpoint":"/api/v1/stores/reviews",
    "status":404,"code":"store_not_found","store_id":"999999"}
  [2026-07-17 10:30:43] production.ERROR: [FAIL] store reviews: store not
    found {"trace_id":"b364d43603a2cee90cdcdfa7677b4c11","correlation_id":
    "affa9da1-7b0f-423f-8d1f-4ccb3378f78c","endpoint":"/api/v1/stores/reviews",
    "status":404,"code":"store_not_found","store_id":"4116"}

Cross-checked against the Flutter-side code (review_controller.dart,
review_screen.dart, git diff read directly):
  - storeReviewList == null && storeReviewError == null -> CircularProgress
    (unchanged "still loading").
  - storeReviewList == null && storeReviewError.code == store_not_found ->
    NearsErrorRetry(kind: notFound), AppLogger.warn (never .failure) ->
    matches AC5 + AC6.
  - storeReviewList != null && isEmpty -> NoDataScreen (unchanged, existing
    ternary branch untouched by the new early-return) -> matches AC4's
    regression requirement (zero-reviews never conflated with not-found).
  - review_not_found_state_test.dart (6/6) + review_controller_test.dart
    (15/15) passed fresh in this QA run (flutter test, 2026-07-17), exercising
    exactly these branches against the real ApiError shapes above.

Verdict for AC4/AC5: marked "unverifiable" (live on-device screen render was
not possible due to the confirmed navigation blocker above) rather than a
silent PASS on tests alone. The backend-contract + code-trace + fresh unit
run above is the strongest evidence available without that entry point.
